{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1516888634,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyOTE1NzgzNTY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2101","origin":"github"},"title":"Add \"collapse\" mode to rerun","message":"Here is the idea as I understand it.  @yarikoptic, please fill in any\nof missing details.\n\nSay we have a branch like this:\n\n```\n---A---B---C---D---E master\n```\n\nAssume A is the first run commit in the line.  If all of these commits\nare run commits that produce the same content (or non-run commits),\nrunning\n\n```\n$ datalad rerun --mode=collapse --since= --onto=\n```\n\nwould give the same branch:\n\n```\n---A---B---C---D---E master\n```\n\nOn the other hand, if C marks the first commit where rerunning the\ncommand leads to different content, running the same command above\nwould result in a tree like this:\n\n```\n         C'---D'---E'  (--branch=NAME or detached)\n        /\n---A---B---C---D---E master\n```\n\nAt this point, even if D and E produce the same content, they happen\nafter the first divergence.\n\nInstead of continuing to extend the diverged branch, we could perhaps\nalso just stop once the first divergence is encountered, and report\nthe diff.\n\nRe: #2076","files":null}]}